#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105478 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105701 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c9317eb-d1ce-5f42-b69b-a37e643b865b" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Vector Projection Using Angle and Magnitude"}] :question/id #uuid "3278333b-a29e-54c5-bc94-b5525bc6f751" :question/math-academy-id "e-14617" :question/problem "Suppose that $|\\,\\mathbf{a}\\,|=8,|\\,\\mathbf{b}\\,|=4$ and that the angle between the vectors is $\\theta = \\dfrac{5\\pi}{6}.$ Find the vector projection of $\\mathbf{a}$ onto $\\mathbf{b}$ in terms of the vector $\\mathbf{b}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the scalar projection as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{b}\\,a & =|\\,a\\,|\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =8\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =8\\cdot (-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}) \\\\  & =-4\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the unit vector that is parallel to $\\mathbf{b}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{u} = \\dfrac{\\mathbf{b}}{|\\,\\mathbf{b}\\,|} = \\dfrac{\\mathbf{b}}{4} = \\dfrac{1}{4} \\mathbf{b}\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute the vector projection as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,a & ={\\text{comp}}_{b}\\,a\\cdot u \\\\  & =-4\\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}b \\\\  & =-\\sqrt{3}b\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105479 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105702 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c0670172-77cb-5e88-b78d-e5136c06095f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Vector Projection Using Components"}] :question/id #uuid "58b2269d-f998-5ba5-9df8-54ea422c43aa" :question/math-academy-id "e-14618" :question/problem "Let $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle 1,-3,5 \\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle 5,-4,0 \\rangle$. Find the vector projection of $\\mathbf{a}$ onto $\\mathbf{b}$." :question/worked-solution "Using the formula for the vector projection, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,a & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{b\\cdot b}b \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z}}{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}+{b}_{z}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 5+(-3)\\cdot (-4)+5\\cdot 0}{{5}^{2}+(-4)^{2}+{0}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{17}{41}⟨5,-4,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{85}{41},-\\frac{68}{41},0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105480 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105703 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "84c96375-27d5-5ada-a952-34e09b3e92bf" :knowledge-point/title "Perpendicular Vectors"}] :question/id #uuid "663f3f5e-56cf-5517-ba1e-d1a355767e0b" :question/math-academy-id "e-14619" :question/problem "Let ![](images/98/984a6c85f7337efcad03af6e6b7af44340243770ade690e383c286154ca9024c.svg) and ![](images/82/825255386c414868f28d139cdc3e50a2b8252fc0c6ad09de579119092afadb9c.svg). Find the vector projection of $\\mathbf{a}$ onto $\\mathbf{b}$." :question/worked-solution "Using the formula for the vector projection, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,a & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{b\\cdot b}b \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z}}{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}+{b}_{z}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 1+0\\cdot 5+1\\cdot (-1)}{{1}^{2}+{5}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{0}{{1}^{2}+{5}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}b \\\\  & =⟨0,0,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186441582 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105701 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c9317eb-d1ce-5f42-b69b-a37e643b865b" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Vector Projection Using Angle and Magnitude"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4f759721-d199-5792-92d1-a10cf5a4cae6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441545} {:answer/id #uuid "915f2842-9a51-5c6a-addd-28d24f144fd1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sqrt{2}c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441554} {:answer/id #uuid "9b92b1e4-60cc-5678-839d-c81bf0c39ab7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441555} {:answer/id #uuid "b52a555e-441d-5b2d-97f8-a2ce1ea1b1a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{2}c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441561} {:answer/id #uuid "e3dc05d9-0a8c-59cb-960f-32824025a367" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441569}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e3dc05d9-0a8c-59cb-960f-32824025a367" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441569} :answer-field/id #uuid "eb9967eb-bff2-51e3-a27a-d037cf218913" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441579}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "30aa8aaa-a9f8-52a5-8c3a-51fa1949b560" :question/math-academy-id "q-101538" :question/problem "Suppose that $|\\,c\\,|=\\sqrt{2}$, $|\\,d\\,|=6$ and that the angle between the vectors is $\\theta ={45}^{∘}.$ Find the vector projection of $d$ onto $c$ in terms of the vector $c.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the scalar projection as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{c}\\,d & =|\\,d\\,|\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =6\\operatorname{cos}⁡({45}^{∘}) \\\\  & =6\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the unit vector that is parallel to $c:$\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{c}{|\\,c\\,|}=\\frac{c}{\\sqrt{2}}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}c\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute the vector projection as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{c}\\,d & ={\\text{comp}}_{c}\\,d\\cdot u \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}c \\\\  & =3c\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186441583 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105702 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c0670172-77cb-5e88-b78d-e5136c06095f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Vector Projection Using Components"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23855489-4a31-5f1e-b065-d3158a58159b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-\\frac{7}{26},-\\frac{35}{26},0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441538} {:answer/id #uuid "2ff64492-2e92-58ae-94ff-14ee9bcf8e67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-\\frac{7}{29},-\\frac{35}{29},0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441540} {:answer/id #uuid "6b914fd7-39d8-59b4-904b-c85d9957296a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{1}{29},\\frac{5}{29},0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441547} {:answer/id #uuid "b1eccb6d-008e-58b0-a553-ceff849b38ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{7}{26},\\frac{35}{26},0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441560} {:answer/id #uuid "c2ffe9f6-07c0-5c84-9abc-3456ff2d160a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-\\frac{1}{26},-\\frac{5}{26},0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441562}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "23855489-4a31-5f1e-b065-d3158a58159b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-\\frac{7}{26},-\\frac{35}{26},0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441538} :answer-field/id #uuid "4b1da517-04d4-5359-b129-b49ab64ce95a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441574}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "35d9ba0b-2c2a-5791-9dcc-879b93c51511" :question/math-academy-id "q-101545" :question/problem "Let $c=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$ and $d=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].$ Find the vector projection of $d$ onto $c.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula for the vector projection, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{c}\\,d & =\\frac{c\\cdot d}{c\\cdot c}c \\\\  & =\\frac{{c}_{x}{d}_{x}+{c}_{y}{d}_{y}+{c}_{z}{d}_{z}}{{c}_{x}^{2}+{c}_{y}^{2}+{c}_{z}^{2}}c \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 3+5\\cdot (-2)+0\\cdot 4}{{1}^{2}+{5}^{2}+{0}^{2}}c \\\\  & =-\\frac{7}{26}⟨1,5,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{7}{26},-\\frac{35}{26},0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186441586 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105701 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c9317eb-d1ce-5f42-b69b-a37e643b865b" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Vector Projection Using Angle and Magnitude"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4898f0e7-39a5-5f06-8e56-8f5aafed918a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "d" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441544} {:answer/id #uuid "8ab5504e-47f2-5106-b694-7a718d03210a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4d" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441552} {:answer/id #uuid "a927a06b-c1ab-5420-bff4-edf63dc12fe1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16d" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441558} {:answer/id #uuid "d281791a-6600-51ff-a350-02e5807be308" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2d" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441567} {:answer/id #uuid "d2a38c14-4542-5cbc-a049-1870202ed396" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8d" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441568}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d281791a-6600-51ff-a350-02e5807be308" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2d" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441567} :answer-field/id #uuid "0478e591-82c4-56f2-9e83-eb51b18b93e3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441571}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a12537f5-cc57-59f7-b432-1391f413c86b" :question/math-academy-id "q-126506" :question/problem "Suppose that $|\\,c\\,|=16$, $|\\,d\\,|=4$ and that the angle between the vectors is $\\theta ={60}^{∘}.$ Find the vector projection of $c$ onto $d$ in terms of the vector $d.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the scalar projection as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{d}\\,c & =|\\,c\\,|\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =16\\operatorname{cos}⁡({60}^{∘}) \\\\  & =16\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the unit vector that is parallel to $d:$\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{d}{|\\,d\\,|}=\\frac{d}{4}=\\frac{1}{4}d\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute the vector projection as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{d}\\,c & ={\\text{comp}}_{d}\\,c\\cdot u \\\\  & =8\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}d \\\\  & =2d\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186441584 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105702 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c0670172-77cb-5e88-b78d-e5136c06095f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Vector Projection Using Components"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "086de454-2713-5601-ab51-799550e139d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨6,2,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441534} {:answer/id #uuid "0b5a1709-5c52-5848-bfee-e95ed0c3f88a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,0,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441536} {:answer/id #uuid "a859db1a-197e-54ad-9642-eb6e745f3fe5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,1,6⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441557} {:answer/id #uuid "ac6f6de5-2f46-5d39-ac3f-cbdff716176a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,6,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441559} {:answer/id #uuid "ce5ad26e-2d08-547a-8436-202ea22b7ccf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4,2,12⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441566}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a859db1a-197e-54ad-9642-eb6e745f3fe5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,1,6⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441557} :answer-field/id #uuid "e210b2c8-4214-56d5-9adf-4f596e3021f5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441578}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "66d2028c-7755-5929-9531-f282efb6ee05" :question/math-academy-id "q-19212" :question/problem "Let $p=⟨2,1,6⟩$ and $q=⟨4,2,12⟩.$ Find the vector projection of $p$ onto $q.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula for the vector projection, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{q}\\,p & =\\frac{p\\cdot q}{q\\cdot q}q \\\\  & =\\frac{{p}_{x}{q}_{x}+{p}_{y}{q}_{y}+{p}_{z}{q}_{z}}{{q}_{x}^{2}+{q}_{y}^{2}+{q}_{z}^{2}}q \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot 4+1\\cdot 2+6\\cdot 12}{{4}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{12}^{2}}q \\\\  & =\\frac{82}{164}⟨4,2,12⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}⟨4,2,12⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,1,6⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186441587 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105702 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c0670172-77cb-5e88-b78d-e5136c06095f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Vector Projection Using Components"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "47726351-7b47-5626-bb7b-c86df88ec37f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,0,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441543} {:answer/id #uuid "5f7f0f17-57fa-52b7-993d-3b6b9a55e712" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{3}{13},0,\\frac{2}{13}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441546} {:answer/id #uuid "6ce967b6-1408-5524-8f74-a23b08c8dddb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{3}{13},\\frac{2}{13},0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441548} {:answer/id #uuid "77159c13-4761-5c51-8623-db6f3303931c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{3}{11},0,\\frac{2}{11}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441550} {:answer/id #uuid "c53001d4-9eb2-5ad7-92c6-63c38e3c778d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{2}{13},0,\\frac{3}{13}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441564}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5f7f0f17-57fa-52b7-993d-3b6b9a55e712" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{3}{13},0,\\frac{2}{13}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441546} :answer-field/id #uuid "bba96ab3-dc17-5fca-8684-49c3032dcc63" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441576}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c0976e49-e373-59e5-b244-6a3f86c33d78" :question/math-academy-id "q-19213" :question/problem "Let $a=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$ and $b=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 14 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].$ Find the vector projection of $b$ onto $a.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula for the vector projection, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{a}\\,b & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{a\\cdot a}a \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z}}{{a}_{x}^{2}+{a}_{y}^{2}+{a}_{z}^{2}}a \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\cdot 1+0\\cdot 14+2\\cdot (-1)}{{3}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{2}^{2}}a \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{13}⟨3,0,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{3}{13},0,\\frac{2}{13}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290297 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105703 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "84c96375-27d5-5ada-a952-34e09b3e92bf" :knowledge-point/title "Perpendicular Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c7ef318-2fcb-5abc-8a64-d58156e31752" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288215} {:answer/id #uuid "5c11b723-d398-54b7-a85d-9a83c61b10d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288673} {:answer/id #uuid "5dc7f785-7e44-5d1c-b5f4-fda66276cfbb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288688} {:answer/id #uuid "9955ee51-0d6d-5dfb-98be-feb9ccd48fbf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289058} {:answer/id #uuid "d81110dc-6d84-5507-8cfa-a7555e54190e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289470}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5c11b723-d398-54b7-a85d-9a83c61b10d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288673} :answer-field/id #uuid "8c5922bf-d851-5e5c-8bcd-35ace642db54" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290040}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6c452b5c-8f3c-5759-a6a2-00c200b73978" :question/math-academy-id "q-212462" :question/problem "Let $a=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$ and $b=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ x\\end{aligned}].$ Given that the projection of $a$ onto $b$ is the zero vector, find the value of $x.$" :question/worked-solution "Since $a$ is a nonzero vector, its projection onto another nonzero vector $b$ equals the zero vector only when the vectors are perpendicular. \n\nSo, we must have\n\n$$\na⊥b\\,⟹\\,a\\cdot b=0.\n$$\n\nComputing the dot product, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & ={a}_{x}\\cdot {b}_{x}+{a}_{y}\\cdot {b}_{y}+{a}_{z}\\cdot {b}_{z} \\\\  & =1\\cdot 1+3\\cdot (-2)+2\\cdot x \\\\  & =2x-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & =0 \\\\ 2x-5 & =0 \\\\ 2x & =5 \\\\ x & =\\frac{5}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186441581 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105703 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "84c96375-27d5-5ada-a952-34e09b3e92bf" :knowledge-point/title "Perpendicular Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27703fdc-dcae-5810-af67-bcf1ab7b205c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441539} {:answer/id #uuid "332eee39-a81f-58e2-9df9-1c8788ae1cd9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441541} {:answer/id #uuid "70d47c6a-00e4-5617-9606-a3844ed20adc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441549} {:answer/id #uuid "866002cd-f732-5473-af59-74d28524c347" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441551} {:answer/id #uuid "c48bc586-6836-5bb9-bad5-ad9ded9e0a14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441563}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c48bc586-6836-5bb9-bad5-ad9ded9e0a14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441563} :answer-field/id #uuid "454a546d-b2cd-5e75-93bf-898cf6aab9d8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441573}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "25a56934-09b0-592a-b002-4f360029a2ea" :question/math-academy-id "q-212463" :question/problem "Let $a=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$ and $b=[\\begin{aligned}11 \\\\ x \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$ Given that the projection of $a$ onto $b$ is the zero vector, find the value of $x.$" :question/worked-solution "Since $a$ is a nonzero vector, its projection onto another nonzero vector $b$ equals the zero vector only when the vectors are perpendicular. \n\nSo, we must have\n\n$$\na⊥b\\,⟹\\,a\\cdot b=0.\n$$\n\nComputing the dot product, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & ={a}_{x}\\cdot {b}_{x}+{a}_{y}\\cdot {b}_{y}+{a}_{z}\\cdot {b}_{z} \\\\  & =0\\cdot 11+4\\cdot x+3\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =4x+6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & =0 \\\\ 4x+6 & =0 \\\\ 4x & =-6 \\\\ x & =-\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186374538 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105703 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "84c96375-27d5-5ada-a952-34e09b3e92bf" :knowledge-point/title "Perpendicular Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10a6363d-50b7-53ee-9211-bf98b3b730c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374540} {:answer/id #uuid "6d50033c-ac1e-5bc6-84ee-1d4b187400c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374541} {:answer/id #uuid "2c9d11de-00b2-5f81-bbb0-9e2cfe2d24d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374542} {:answer/id #uuid "4f93f9db-ba0a-508a-846f-8f31e1eda3c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374543} {:answer/id #uuid "4bade5c1-6626-584d-87f1-ee5499c60e01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374544}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4f93f9db-ba0a-508a-846f-8f31e1eda3c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374543} :answer-field/id #uuid "af73e53b-f8ec-53d4-ad2f-688f3fcd26ab" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374539}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cfdc0ea6-159a-5bd6-ad02-2e0fd2db5b29" :question/math-academy-id "q-212464" :question/problem "Let $a=[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$ and $b=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ x \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].$ Given that the projection of $a$ onto $b$ is the zero vector, find the value of $x.$" :question/worked-solution "Since $a$ is a nonzero vector, its projection onto another nonzero vector $b$ equals the zero vector only when the vectors are perpendicular. \n\nSo, we must have\n\n$$\na⊥b\\,⟹\\,a\\cdot b=0.\n$$\n\nComputing the dot product, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & ={a}_{x}\\cdot {b}_{x}+{a}_{y}\\cdot {b}_{y}+{a}_{z}\\cdot {b}_{z} \\\\  & =-6\\cdot (-2)+(-3)\\cdot x+0\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =12-3x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & =0 \\\\ 12-3x & =0 \\\\ -3x & =-12 \\\\ x & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186441588 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105703 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "84c96375-27d5-5ada-a952-34e09b3e92bf" :knowledge-point/title "Perpendicular Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "192f30d7-4e5b-597c-b16e-383b0b641a0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441537} {:answer/id #uuid "8aba8f71-12dd-51aa-a5d5-f2bf983e166b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441553} {:answer/id #uuid "9ee90094-51ba-5008-b5eb-89abf0073014" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441556} {:answer/id #uuid "cbf3bc6d-a5c0-5131-be8c-1f828fbf1aa2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441565} {:answer/id #uuid "efe3cfb8-92c2-5e3a-b874-10f960d8adca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441570}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9ee90094-51ba-5008-b5eb-89abf0073014" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441556} :answer-field/id #uuid "acb824ea-82ae-5e97-acfd-078323166d84" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441575}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fc72b4b3-1726-5899-88e5-9bd9e302a6a9" :question/math-academy-id "q-212469" :question/problem "Let $a=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ and $b=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ 5 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].$ Given that the projection of $a$ onto $b$ is the zero vector, find the value of $x.$" :question/worked-solution "Since $a$ is a nonzero vector, its projection onto another nonzero vector $b$ equals the zero vector only when the vectors are perpendicular. \n\nSo, we must have\n\n$$\na⊥b\\,⟹\\,a\\cdot b=0.\n$$\n\nComputing the dot product, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & ={a}_{x}\\cdot {b}_{x}+{a}_{y}\\cdot {b}_{y}+{a}_{z}\\cdot {b}_{z} \\\\  & =4\\cdot x+(-4)\\cdot 5+1\\cdot (-4) \\\\  & =4x-24.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & =0 \\\\ 4x-24 & =0 \\\\ 4x & =24 \\\\ x & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186441585 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105701 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c9317eb-d1ce-5f42-b69b-a37e643b865b" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Vector Projection Using Angle and Magnitude"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a7d4837-c858-547a-810b-4a932bb463f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441542}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3a7d4837-c858-547a-810b-4a932bb463f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441542} :answer-field/id #uuid "d497f000-d7bf-588c-ad25-93aa61c11659" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441577}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8e5a64ce-22c5-5e8c-997a-c2e3826ce849" :question/math-academy-id "q-275227" :question/problem "Suppose that $|\\,a\\,|=16$, $|\\,b\\,|=2$ and that the angle between the vectors is $\\theta =\\frac{2\\pi }{3}.$ Find the vector projection of $a$ onto $b$ in terms of the vector $b.$\n\n${\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,a=$\n{{field-1}}\n$b$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the scalar projection as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{b}\\,a & =|\\,a\\,|\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =16\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =16\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the unit vector that is parallel to $b:$\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{b}{|\\,b\\,|}=\\frac{b}{2}=\\frac{1}{2}b\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute the vector projection as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,a & ={\\text{comp}}_{b}\\,a\\cdot u \\\\  & =-8\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}b \\\\  & =-4\\,b.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186441580 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105701 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c9317eb-d1ce-5f42-b69b-a37e643b865b" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Vector Projection Using Angle and Magnitude"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ae82f23-3f33-55f8-b143-c4e2aa44358a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441535}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0ae82f23-3f33-55f8-b143-c4e2aa44358a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441535} :answer-field/id #uuid "42723228-7b18-5999-8f79-63b014252842" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441572}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "24948042-4caf-54ad-85ae-20d1f75949ff" :question/math-academy-id "q-316438" :question/problem "Suppose that $|\\,x\\,|=9$, $|\\,y\\,|=6$ and that the angle between the vectors is $\\theta =\\pi .$ Find the vector projection of $x$ onto $y$ in terms of the vector $y.$\n\n${\\text{proj}}_{y}\\,x=$\n{{field-1}}\n$y$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the scalar projection as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{y}\\,x & =|\\,x\\,|\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =9\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi ) \\\\  & =9\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =-9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the unit vector that is parallel to $y:$\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{y}{|\\,y\\,|}=\\frac{y}{6}=\\frac{1}{6}y\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute the vector projection as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{y}\\,x & ={\\text{comp}}_{y}\\,x\\cdot u \\\\  & =-9\\cdot \\frac{1}{6}y \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}\\,y\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299634 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105702 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c0670172-77cb-5e88-b78d-e5136c06095f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Vector Projection Using Components"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e9d61422-1475-5621-ad7d-a849aaca114f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298546}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e9d61422-1475-5621-ad7d-a849aaca114f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298546} :answer-field/id #uuid "0984c5b8-6bfe-56e8-9582-60026aa3bd96" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298667} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c9f7fec6-5215-539e-8f83-5634b3c4076a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{34}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298431}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c9f7fec6-5215-539e-8f83-5634b3c4076a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{34}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298431} :answer-field/id #uuid "0e38d24f-0d2e-5b55-b975-90a7ef2d3a53" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298686} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24aadbe1-8097-598a-9d4b-d9e79efcd1e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{17}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297709}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "24aadbe1-8097-598a-9d4b-d9e79efcd1e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{17}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297709} :answer-field/id #uuid "9689e94a-473b-55d0-80de-83ad1a852f62" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299134}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0810600b-ad06-5852-ade5-064bb8170efd" :question/math-academy-id "q-317655" :question/problem "Let $r=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]$ and $s=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].$ Find the vector projection of $r$ onto $s.$\n\n${\\text{proj}}_{s}\\,r=⟨$ \n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$,$\n{{field-3}}\n$⟩$" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula for the vector projection, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{s}\\,r & =\\frac{r\\cdot s}{s\\cdot s}s \\\\  & =\\frac{{r}_{x}{s}_{x}+{r}_{y}{s}_{y}+{r}_{z}{s}_{z}}{{s}_{x}^{2}+{s}_{y}^{2}+{s}_{z}^{2}}s \\\\  & =\\frac{(-3)\\cdot 1+2\\cdot 0+7\\cdot (-2)}{{1}^{2}+{0}^{2}+(-2)^{2}}s \\\\  & =\\frac{-17}{5}⟨1,0,-2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\,-\\frac{17}{5},0,\\frac{34}{5}\\,⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299636 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105702 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c0670172-77cb-5e88-b78d-e5136c06095f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Vector Projection Using Components"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "406c9253-8200-5ad3-8d4b-33726202a988" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{23}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297809}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "406c9253-8200-5ad3-8d4b-33726202a988" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{23}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297809} :answer-field/id #uuid "5d8666c5-0963-50a4-bc97-4b5c38053501" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298959} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1df406d7-a2cd-566a-9e5c-dbf376476be5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{23}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297681}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1df406d7-a2cd-566a-9e5c-dbf376476be5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{23}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297681} :answer-field/id #uuid "d08d1232-d14d-502d-8d1a-ea40bec46176" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299341} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "74ad9205-623c-5b5c-8b1b-874ef60380c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{23}{30}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298055}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "74ad9205-623c-5b5c-8b1b-874ef60380c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{23}{30}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298055} :answer-field/id #uuid "e9147c73-f105-5d8b-83ed-2692f2208968" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299426}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1656678a-52ed-5990-af8d-fd8bfe8d48c4" :question/math-academy-id "q-317658" :question/problem "Let $c=⟨-2,1,5⟩$ and $d=⟨4,0,-3⟩.$ Find the vector projection of $d$ onto $c.$\n\n${\\text{proj}}_{c}\\,d=⟨$\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$,$\n{{field-3}}\n$⟩$" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula for the vector projection, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{c}\\,d & =\\frac{c\\cdot d}{c\\cdot c}c \\\\  & =\\frac{{c}_{x}{d}_{x}+{c}_{y}{d}_{y}+{c}_{z}{d}_{z}}{{c}_{x}^{2}+{c}_{y}^{2}+{c}_{z}^{2}}c \\\\  & =\\frac{(-2)\\cdot 4+1\\cdot 0+5\\cdot (-3)}{(-2)^{2}+{1}^{2}+{5}^{2}}c \\\\  & =\\frac{-8+0-15}{4+1+25}⟨-2,1,5⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{-23}{30}⟨-2,1,5⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\,\\frac{23}{15},-\\frac{23}{30},-\\frac{23}{6}\\,⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299663 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105703 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "84c96375-27d5-5ada-a952-34e09b3e92bf" :knowledge-point/title "Perpendicular Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fa759f3a-59cf-57f1-9eb4-fe076883ee65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298620}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fa759f3a-59cf-57f1-9eb4-fe076883ee65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298620} :answer-field/id #uuid "415cdd53-3c35-5e12-a9ad-bdb260275079" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298863}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2940b787-7de0-58e6-a5d9-3477f08d2d69" :question/math-academy-id "q-317944" :question/problem "Let $a=t\\,i-4j+k$ and $b=4i+j.$ Given that the projection of $a$ onto $b$ is the zero vector, find the value of $t.$\n\n$t=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Since $a$ is a nonzero vector, its projection onto another nonzero vector $b$ equals the zero vector only when the vectors are perpendicular.\n\nSo, we must have\n\n$$\na⊥b\\,⟹\\,a\\cdot b=0.\n$$\n\nComputing the dot product, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & ={a}_{x}\\cdot {b}_{x}+{a}_{y}\\cdot {b}_{y}+{a}_{z}\\cdot {b}_{z} \\\\  & =t\\cdot 4+(-4)\\cdot 1+1\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =4t-4+0 \\\\  & =4t-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & =0 \\\\ 4t-4 & =0 \\\\ 4t & =4 \\\\ t & =1 \\\\ t & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106480 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105701 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c9317eb-d1ce-5f42-b69b-a37e643b865b" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Vector Projection Using Angle and Magnitude"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9c46506b-71f4-5dd4-8073-f478001468d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186105029} {:answer/id #uuid "aa28895b-01c4-5a6a-8497-a8805ff0c18e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186105030} {:answer/id #uuid "0bd413b9-0ccc-5243-898a-0e04480488f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186105031} {:answer/id #uuid "371bec7c-71dd-546e-8bff-407c6e758672" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{4}c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186105032} {:answer/id #uuid "7c124655-5867-56b0-ab0d-79de478b24e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186105033}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0bd413b9-0ccc-5243-898a-0e04480488f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186105031} :answer-field/id #uuid "295493ed-d510-566e-997d-2641481e7989" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186105028}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e48c0a41-451d-5386-8afe-32a1dfe30bdb" :question/math-academy-id "q-71836" :question/problem "Suppose that $|\\,c\\,|=12$, $|\\,d\\,|=6$ and that the angle between the vectors is $\\theta =\\frac{2\\pi }{3}.$ Find the vector projection of $d$ onto $c$ in terms of the vector $c.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the scalar projection as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{c}\\,d & =|\\,d\\,|\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =6\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =6\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the unit vector that is parallel to $c:$\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{c}{|\\,c\\,|}=\\frac{c}{12}=\\frac{1}{12}c\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute the vector projection as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{c}\\,d & ={\\text{comp}}_{c}\\,d\\cdot u \\\\  & =(-3)\\cdot \\frac{1}{12}c \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}c\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
